{"slug": "rainbow-quinoa-salad", "nyt_id": 1016222, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1016222-rainbow-quinoa-salad", "name": "Rainbow Quinoa Salad", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "Dr. David Eisenberg of the Harvard School of Public Health demonstrated along with his daughter, Naomi, a whole- wheat couscous salad that is the inspiration for this one at the “Healthy Kitchens, Healthy Lives” medical education conference in Napa Valley this year. You can use a variety of dried fruits and nuts, as well as a mix of herbs. Chop the larger dried fruits small so that the pieces are uniform.", "servings": {"text": "6 to 8 servings", "min": 6, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 35, "raw": {"total": "PT35M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "4 cups water", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "⅔ cup chopped dried fruit (such as apricots, raisins, cranberries, figs, currants)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.6666666666666666, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped dried fruit (such as apricots", "preparation": "raisins, cranberries, figs, currants)", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¼ cup chopped cilantro", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped cilantro", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "¼ cup chopped fresh mint", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped fresh mint", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "½ cup chopped fresh parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped fresh parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 cup red quinoa or rainbow quinoa, rinsed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "red quinoa or rainbow quinoa", "preparation": "rinsed", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "¼ cup lightly toasted pistachios", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "lightly toasted pistachios", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "¼ cup lightly toasted almonds, chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "lightly toasted almonds", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "¼ cup chopped walnuts", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped walnuts", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 teaspoons lemon zest", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "lemon zest", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "¼ cup fresh lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "fresh lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "1 small garlic clove, puréeed (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "small garlic clove", "preparation": "puréeed (optional)", "optional": true}, {"position": 15, "raw": "¼ teaspoon ground cinnamon", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cinnamon", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "1 teaspoon pomegranate molasses", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "pomegranate molasses", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "⅓ cup extra- virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra- virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Bring water to a boil in a 3-quart saucepan and add quinoa and salt to taste. Bring back to a rolling boil, then reduce heat slightly and boil gently for 20 minutes, or until you see a thread emerge from the blond and red quinoa. Drain and shake well in the strainer, then return to pot. Cover pot with a dishtowel and then , then place a lid over the dishtowel and let sit for 10 to 15 minutes undisturbed. Transfer to a large bowl."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Meanwhile, whisk together lemon juice, salt, garlic, cinnamon, and pomegranate molasses. Whisk in olive oil."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Toss together quinoa and dressing. Add remaining ingredients and toss together. Transfer to a platter, a wide bowl or individual plates and serve."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 268.625, "protein_g": 6.0, "carbohydrates_g": 26.2, "fat_g": 16.9, "saturated_fat_g": 2.0, "unsaturated_fat_g": 4.6, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": null, "sodium_mg": 442.2, "fiber_g": 4.2, "sugar_g": 7.1, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mediterranean"], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer-dinner-lunch-main-course-salad"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["fall", "spring", "summer", "winter"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/05/science/09recipehealth/09recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/05/science/09recipehealth/09recipehealth-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 2189}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2014-04-04", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:06:00Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "raspberry-champagne-soup-with-rosemary-raspberry-sorbet", "nyt_id": 10026, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10026-raspberry-champagne-soup-with-rosemary-raspberry-sorbet", "name": "Raspberry-Champagne Soup With Rosemary- Raspberry Sorbet", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 90, "raw": {"total": "PT1H30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 cup sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ cup water", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 ½ pints fresh raspberries", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "pint", "item": "fresh raspberries", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 tablespoons balsamic vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "balsamic vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 ½ tablespoons chopped fresh rosemary", "group": null, "quantity": 2.5, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh rosemary", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ cup sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup water", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 ½ pints fresh raspberries", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "pint", "item": "fresh raspberries", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 cups good-quality Champagne or other sparkling wine, chilled", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "good-quality champagne or other sparkling wine", "preparation": "chilled", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "To make the sorbet, combine the sugar and water in a small saucepan over medium heat. Simmer for 5 minutes and set aside to cool. Place the raspberries, sugar syrup, vinegar and rosemary in a blender and puree until smooth. Let stand for 1 hour. Strain through a fine-mesh sieve. Refrigerate until cold. Freeze according to the directions on your ice-cream machine."}, {"position": 2, "text": "To make the soup, combine the sugar and water in a small saucepan over medium heat. Simmer just until the sugar dissolves. Let cool. Place all but one-half cup of the raspberries in a blender with the sugar syrup. Puree until smooth. Strain through a fine mesh sieve and refrigerate until cold."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Just before serving, divide the soup mixture among four bowls and add one-half cup of Champagne to each. Place a scoop of the sorbet in the soup and garnish with the remaining raspberries."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 516.75, "protein_g": 3.0, "carbohydrates_g": 107.5, "fat_g": 1.6, "saturated_fat_g": 0.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.9, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": null, "sodium_mg": 13.5, "fiber_g": 15.4, "sugar_g": 87.5, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dessert-sorbet-soup"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["champagne", "fall", "raspberry", "rosemary", "summer"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": null, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1996-06-02", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:26:26Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
